      "claim_id": "innodb-8-4-transaction-concurrency-default",
      "text": "MySQL 8.4 documents InnoDB as the default storage engine, with ACID DML including commit, rollback and crash recovery, row-level locking, consistent reads, and foreign-key support.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql-8-4-innodb-intro"],
      "answer_locations": ["核心结论", "1 分钟版", "3 分钟版", "原理机制", "常见追问", "易错点"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "innodb-clustered-secondary-indexes",
      "text": "MySQL 8.4 documents that each InnoDB table has a clustered index storing row data; a primary key is used when defined, otherwise a suitable NOT NULL unique index or hidden 6-byte row-ID index is used. Secondary records include primary-key columns and use them to find rows in the clustered index; long primary keys increase secondary-index space.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql-8-4-innodb-indexes"],
      "answer_locations": ["核心结论", "1 分钟版", "3 分钟版", "关键细节", "原理机制", "常见追问", "易错点"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "myisam-8-4-capabilities-and-files",
      "text": "MySQL 8.4 documents that MyISAM has B-tree indexes but no clustered indexes, transactions, foreign-key support or MVCC; its locking granularity is table, it stores data in .MYD and indexes in .MYI, and it can check/repair improperly closed tables when configured with myisam_recover_options.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql-8-4-myisam"],
